cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research software, please cite the software release and the
  prior methods relevant to the components you use; canonical references are
  listed in references.bib.
title: "Interaction-Uncertainty: A Prompt-Conditioned Belief-to-Primitive Bridge"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Interactive Perception Research Team"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-04
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A model-agnostic, fixed-camera research interface that converts
  prompt-conditioned task beliefs and action-conditioned outcome predictions
  into grounded interactive-manipulation or information-enrichment primitives,
  without exposing simulator-privileged semantic identifiers to the policy.
keywords:
  - interactive perception
  - robot manipulation
  - uncertainty quantification
  - Bayes risk
  - vision-language-action models
  - benchmark
